  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with MAP/microtubule affinity-regulating kinase 4 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Oblonganoside C to K-252a, which in turn targets MAP/microtubule affinity-regulating kinase 4, suggesting a direct inhibitory effect on the kinase. The second pathway connects Oblonganoside C to SBK1, which is targeted by benzocaine, and both SBK1 and benzocaine are implicated in targeting the same kinase. The third pathway reveals a more complex interaction, where Oblonganoside C targets Tyrosine-protein kinase Fes/Fps, which is inhibited by a complex compound, and this complex ultimately affects the kinase of interest. These findings collectively suggest that Oblonganoside C may modulate the activity of MAP/microtubule affinity-regulating kinase 4 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving kinase inhibition or regulatory signaling pathways. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
